For text without newlines (single line): output is `>` + hints + linebreak + indent + text with wrapping at width 80 (words split at spaces). Wrapping: words are kept whole; a break happens at a space when the column exceeds best_width (80). The space at break is consumed and replaced by line break + indent.

For text with newlines: breaks are preserved (each `\n` in text produces line break in output), blank lines preserved. Paragraph structure maintained.

